even during a pandemic when fewer of us  are on the road  one unfortunate statistic is still  climbing pedestrian deaths in the valley  they're up 30 percent from last year  today local police are coming together  though to try and promote  crosswalk safety kate houston live at  flamingo in mojave with a look at how to  keep you and your family safe  kate police say that flamingo road is  one of the most dangerous streets for  pedestrians  behind me here you can see there is a  marked crosswalk it even has some  flashing  lights and a sign that says pedestrian  crossing  now with that said we still saw many  people drive through it as  officers were trying to cross this  morning as part of the annual turkey  crossing  a metro officer wore a sparkly turkey  costume  as he attempted to cross the street  police say if drivers won't stop for  this  along with the flashing crosswalk lights  how will they stop for a child or  another person  there have been 56 pedestrian deaths  this year that's  six more lives than last year at this  time metro police are urging drivers to  be aware of their surroundings  especially on roads like flamingo which  allows drivers to go 45 miles per hour  every single one of those persons have  you know they're somebody's child or  somebody's parent  it's unfortunate drivers just slow down  you know it's not worth  getting there 10 seconds early or even a  couple minutes early  metro police say 80 percent of  pedestrian deaths happened between dusk  and dawn walkers are encouraged to wear  bright clothes or  reflective bands on their clothing  police say pedestrians should make eye  contact with drivers before entering a  crosswalk  and clear each lane before moving  forward  today police gave out 123 citations  to drivers who did not stop during the  safety event  one person was arrested for driving  under the influence  reporting from flamingo mojave kate  houston 8 news now
 

